    "recommendations": "• Install a reflective address marker at the driveway entrance so responders can locate the property quickly from the road.\n• Mark the driveway entrance with posts or reflective delineators on both sides to define the entry point under low-light or smoky conditions.\n• Create a designated turnaround area near the residence large enough for fire apparatus and ambulances to reverse direction without backing the full length of the driveway.\n• Keep the full width of the access drive clear of parked vehicles, equipment, and vegetation so apparatus can reach the residence without obstruction.\n• Identify and mark a secondary parking area away from the residence where arriving responders can stage vehicles without blocking the access drive.\n• Keep the parking area near the residence clear during emergencies so the closest approach to the structure remains open for fire and medical apparatus.\n• Trim any vegetation along the access drive that reduces vertical or horizontal clearance for large emergency vehicles.\n• Post the property address visibly at the residence itself in addition to the driveway entrance, so responders who reach the building can confirm the correct location."
